# Product Certification Kit

Canonical: `docs/DEV.md` § Product Certification Kit; runner `scripts/product-cert.sh`.

## Why

Play rejected Khaynjo for **Broken Functionality** (opens then crashes). Sidebar
and silent background errors also made the UI glitchy. Cert exists so those
classes of failure **block ship**.

## Do

```bash
./scripts/product-cert.sh --tier=fast          # before claiming a UI/layout fix
./scripts/product-cert.sh --tier=full <app>    # before Linux package
./scripts/product-cert.sh --tier=store <app>   # before Play / MSIX / MSI upload
```

## Do not

- Upload Play AAB / MSIX / MSI / AUR without a green cert for that app
- Skip launch-to-stable or sidebar smoke when changing chrome / Android insets / panic handling
- Treat “process still has a pid” as a launch pass — Android smoke must also fail on ANR/FATAL and on pid-alive-without-resumed-UI; store tier must not skip device smoke without `CERT_ALLOW_ANDROID_SKIP=1`
- Cert Android against the **local makepad APK only** — Play ships the **AAB**. Store/android smoke must install an AAB-derived universal/device APK (bundletool) and prefer a USB arm device over an x86 emulator. `android_assert_aab_launch_bg` must see `MakepadLaunchBg` in the AAB dex (aapt vs aapt2 R-id drift otherwise crashes onCreate on API 26 as `id/menu_copy`)
- Use Python for new cert tooling (bash only)
